      },
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.7,
          "end": 6.82,
          "en": "That is it for stores. Also check out the lecture after this lecture where I also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.82,
          "end": 9.2,
          "en": "prepared some additional things you can do with stores.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.48,
          "end": 15.14,
          "en": "But the main thing about stores is that you can create writable and readable stores.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 16.52,
          "end": 20.7,
          "en": "Readable stores are great for pieces of data that update automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 21.22,
          "end": 27.26,
          "en": "Writable stores will be the main stores you interact with because they allow you to both subscribe to them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 27.26,
          "end": 29.82,
          "en": "and trigger changes in the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 32.32,
          "en": "manually based on user events and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 32.58,
          "end": 34.68,
          "en": "And you also learned about custom stores,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 34.98,
          "end": 38.18,
          "en": "which is a useful enhancement for writable stores,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 38.18,
          "end": 43.1,
          "en": "where you can hide away some of the complexity from your components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 43.1,
          "end": 45.14,
          "en": "and put it into the store file instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 45.14,
          "end": 46.9,
          "en": "and have all your heavy lifting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 47.12,
          "end": 48.68,
          "en": "all your logic in the store file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.8,
          "end": 49.68,
          "en": "And in the components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.68,
          "end": 53.22,
          "en": "you can just call easy to use methods like remove item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.22,
          "end": 55.3,
          "en": "and all the magic happens behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.3,
          "end": 62.12,
          "en": "Stores are super useful features in Svelte because they allow you to outsource logic and most",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.12,
          "end": 65.14,
          "en": "importantly data management into dedicated files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.4,
          "end": 70.28,
          "en": "They make sure that you don't have infinitely long prop and custom event chains.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 70.52,
          "end": 79.1,
          "en": "And they particularly make communicating between loosely related components like the product and the cart component here much easier.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
